# Google Ads sitelink "Bestselling Books" was built against /best-sellers, but
# the generated landing page is /bestsellers/ (no hyphen). The asset was
# disapproved "Destination not working — HTTP 404" and stopped serving. Google
# re-checks automatically, so redirecting is a faster and more durable fix than
# editing the asset: any future ad, email or partner link using the hyphenated
# spelling lands correctly too.
/best-sellers/   /bestsellers/  301
/best-sellers    /bestsellers/  301
/best-seller/    /bestsellers/  301
/best-seller     /bestsellers/  301
/bestseller/     /bestsellers/  301
/bestseller      /bestsellers/  301


# Client-rendered listing pages
/category/*    /category/    200
/collection/*  /collection/  200


# No catch-all: Pages serves the generated 404.html for anything unmatched.
# That keeps admin-created product pages (whose Lambda is not ported yet) out
# of the index as real 404s instead of soft-200 duplicate homepages.
